.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_BODY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_body \- access the buffered request body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const void *chttpsvr_req_body(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                               size_t *len_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a pointer to the buffered bytes of the request body.  It
stores the body length in bytes in len_out, when len_out is not NULL.
It returns NULL and stores 0 in two cases: the request has no body, or
req belongs to a streaming route that
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler registered.  The server never
extracts the body of a streaming route in advance.  Use
chttpsvr_req_read for such a route.

The buffer stays valid for the length of the handler call.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
